{
  "key": "HMA-401957",
  "summary": "Basic Multi-armed Bandit option for A/B testing",
  "type": "Story",
  "priority": "Medium",
  "status": "In Development",
  "assignee": "Sachin Bansal",
  "reporter": "Su Su",
  "created": "2026-01-26T10:01:17.564-0500",
  "updated": "2026-06-25T01:03:31.449-0400",
  "components": [],
  "labels": [],
  "fixVersions": [],
  "description": {
    "type": "doc",
    "version": 1,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In addition to existing options in A/B testing for selecting the branch, we will add multi-armed bandit ("
          },
          {
            "type": "inlineCard",
            "attrs": {
              "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-armed_bandit"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " ) as a move towards integrating more AI capability, even though we only implement the basic case."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "To do this, the below new configuration settings are added to A/B test UI"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "order": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Threshold on total presentation of all the branches."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Minimum percentage (minPer) to be selected for for random selection."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This is how it works"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "order": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Initially, the branches are selected randomly based on the initial configured percentage"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "When the threshold is reached, the random selection is applied in only minPercentage of the cases; while the branch with the highest acceptance rate is selected for the rest. For example, if minPer=10, random selection is applied in 10% of the getOffers call, and the best performant branch is selected in 90% of the cases."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The best performant branch is dynamically evaluated, although not necessarily for every getOffers call. The evaluation for best offer should consider the recent data rather than considering the contact & accept counts from the beginning. The logic for “recent data“ is to be decided."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "descriptionText": "<p>In addition to existing options in A/B testing for selecting the branch, we will add multi-armed bandit (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-armed_bandit\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multi-armed_bandit</a> ) as a move towards integrating more AI capability, even though we only implement the basic case.</p>\n\n<p>To do this, the below new configuration settings are added to A/B test UI</p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Threshold on total presentation of all the branches.</li>\n\t<li>Minimum percentage (minPer) to be selected for for random selection.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<p>This is how it works</p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Initially, the branches are selected randomly based on the initial configured percentage</li>\n\t<li>When the threshold is reached, the random selection is applied in only minPercentage of the cases; while the branch with the highest acceptance rate is selected for the rest. For example, if minPer=10, random selection is applied in 10% of the getOffers call, and the best performant branch is selected in 90% of the cases.</li>\n\t<li>The best performant branch is dynamically evaluated, although not necessarily for every getOffers call. The evaluation for best offer should consider the recent data rather than considering the contact &amp; accept counts from the beginning. The logic for “recent data“ is to be decided.</li>\n</ol>\n",
